|\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}|=\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(2)^{2}}=\sqrt{16+4}=\sqrt{20}

Since, $|\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}|=|\mathbf{a}||\mathbf{b}| \sin \theta$,
If $\theta$ is angle between $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$.

\begin{aligned}
\sqrt{20} &=\sqrt{9+1+4} \sqrt{1+1+4} \sin \theta \\
\Rightarrow \sin \theta &=\frac{\sqrt{20}}{\sqrt{6} \sqrt{14}} \\
